      "- Highlight deals that smell wrong (e.g., \"in late stage but no meeting in 30 days\")",
      "You still want human override: - Reps and managers can adjust probabilities based on real context - Leadership can factor in strategic deals where model has little history",
      "But you start conversations from: - \"Model says 4.8 crores is realistic this quarter; why do you think it's 7?\" not - \"Everyone please give me your best guess.\"",
      "The result is: - Less surprise - Fewer wild swings - More trust in the numbers",
      "Step 6: Learning From Wins and Losses - Sharpening the Blade",
      "Every deal is feedback from the market.",
