      "product experience. - High-intent signals get routed to sales with",
      "context, not dumped as cold leads. - Learning",
      "- Experiments are logged with hypothesis, setup, result, and lesson.",
      "- AI helps summarise and pattern-match across tests.",
      "- Every quarter, key learnings feed back into: - Personas - Messaging - Channel strategy - Product feedback You don't need a huge team or budget for this. You need clarity, focus, and sensible use of AI.",
      "Where AI Marketing Goes Wrong (So You Can Avoid It)",
      "1. Content factories with no strategy - Teams churn out endless AI-generated posts. - No clear audience, message, or desired",
      "behaviour change. 1. Result: lots of noise, little impact.  Counter: - For every piece of content, ask: - Who is this for? - What do we want them to do or feel? - How will we know if it worked? 1. Vanity metrics obsession - AI helps maximise impressions, clicks, followers. - No link to pipeline or revenue. 1. Counter: - Tie campaigns to: - Qualified leads",
      "- Opportunities created - Revenue influence (where traceable) - Treat likes and shares as leading indicators,",
      "not success. 1. Ignoring downstream teams - Marketing generates more leads with AI. - Sales and support drown. - Lead quality drops. - Internal friction rises. 1. Counter: - Design journeys jointly with sales and support. - Agree on: - Lead definitions - Handover rules - Feedback loops (\"these leads are useless\" fix",
      "upstream). 1. Compliance and brand risk - AI hallucinations lead to wrong claims. - Customised messages accidentally promise",
      "things you can't do. 1. Counter: - Pre-approve core claims and value propositions. - Restrict AI from inventing facts. - Review high-exposure content carefully.",
      "The Leadership Role in AI-Enabled Marketing",
      "You do not need to know how any of the tools work under the hood.",
      "You do need to set expectations and boundaries. Ask your marketing leader:",
      "1. \"Show me how we're using AI today in: - Understanding customers - Creating content - Targeting and journeys - Testing and learning\" 1. \"Which experiments have we run in the last 6",
