      "Part 1: Fixing Support - From Firefighting to Intelligent Triage",
      "Most support teams live in permanent fire mode. - Big queues - Angry customers - Stressed agents - Leaders begging for more headcount or fewer promises",
      "Let's apply the company brain.",
      "1. Memory: Knowing the Customer in Front of You Right now, a typical agent sees:",
      "- The current ticket - Maybe a few recent tickets - If motivated, a CRM record in another tab They usually do not see: - Contract details and commitments - History of incidents and past promises - Current projects and open opportunities - Product usage patterns AI, sitting on top of a connected memory layer, can change that. When a ticket appears, the system can assemble a context panel:",
      "- Who this customer is (segment, value, contract tier)",
