      "Part 2: Elevating Success - From Relationship Management to Value Management",
      "Customer Success often has a vague mandate:",
      "- \"Own the relationship.\" - \"Drive adoption.\" - \"Prevent churn.\" Which can mean anything... and therefore often means nothing concrete.",
      "Let's make it sharp.",
      "Success should exist to:",
      "1. Ensure customers actually realise the outcomes they bought you for",
