      "- Increase frustration while saving pennies Simple rules for sane bot usage:",
      "1. Be honest - Make it clear when customers are talking to a",
      "bot. - Don't fake names and photos. 1. Give a clear escape hatch - \"Talk to a human\" should always be an option",
      "within a few steps. - Escalation should carry context (ticket history,",
      "what was already tried). 1. Start with narrow scopes - FAQs - Order/status queries - Password, billing basics 1. Only expand when performance is proven. 2. Loop learning back - Analyse where the bot fails or where humans",
      "override it. - Improve flows and knowledge accordingly. Bots are tools, not gatekeepers. Use them to remove friction, not to hide from customers.",
      "KPIs That Actually Matter in AI-Enabled Support & Success",
      "With AI in the mix, you'll see tool vendors flaunt new metrics.",
      "Keep your eyes on the ones that matter:",
      "Support",
      "- Time to first response (by segment / severity) - Time to resolution - Re-open rate (issues not really fixed) - Volume per customer segment (are certain",
