      "without hurting satisfaction Success",
      "- Net revenue retention (NRR) - Gross churn (logo and revenue) - Expansion by segment and cohort - Health score trends (and their correlation with",
      "actual churn/expansion) - Time-to-value for new customers (time to first",
      "meaningful outcome) AI's job is to:",
      "- Push these in the right direction - Reduce variance - Make your capacity go further If you're adding AI and these metrics don't improve over time, you're just adding complexity.",
      "The Human Side: Empathy and Authority",
      "Support and Success live at the emotional front line.",
      "Two things AI cannot replace:",
      "1. Genuine empathy - Recognising the human on the other side - Handling anger without escalating it",
      "- Knowing when to say, \"Let me take ownership of this and get back to you.\"",
      "1. Real authority - The ability to actually fix things: - Approve a workaround - Push internally - Offer a concession when justified If your AI initiatives strip agents and CSMs of autonomy and turn them into script-approvers, you will burn them out and annoy customers.",
      "Use AI to: - Give them better information - Remove boring documentation work - Suggest options",
      "Then empower them to: - Make calls within clear boundaries - Escalate quickly when needed - Spend more time in high-value interactions (complex issues, strategic accounts)",
      "What a Sane AI-Enabled Support & Success Engine Looks Like",
      "Let's combine it.",
      "Support - Tickets arrive. AI: - Classifies, prioritises, and routes - Pulls context and shows it to the agent - Suggests responses and playbooks",
      "- Simple issues: - Resolved via AI or agent+AI in a single",
      "interaction - Complex issues: - Escalated with full history attached - Incident patterns identified and fed to",
      "product/ops - Leadership: - Sees clear dashboards of volume, themes, time,",
      "and satisfaction - Uses insights to drive upstream fixes Success",
      "- At onboarding: - Success outcomes are defined and captured - AI summarises and tracks against them - During the relationship: - AI monitors health signals and usage - CSMs are alerted to risk and opportunity - Quarterly reviews are prepared with AI-",
      "generated, human-checked briefs - For expansion: - AI identifies likely candidates based on patterns - CSMs approach with data-backed proposals - For learning: - Churn and expansion are analysed - Insights feed back into: - Product - Sales promises - Onboarding",
      "- Support workflows Support and Success stop being \"post-sale overhead\" and become central loops in your company brain.",
      "Flight Exercise: Your 90-Day Support",
      "& Success Upgrade",
      "Let's make this practical. Take 15-20 minutes and sketch one focused upgrade. 1. Choose the Primary Pain Complete:",
      "\"Right now, the most painful problem in our post-sale experience is _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _.\" Examples: - Slow or inconsistent support responses - Same issues happening again and again - Poor onboarding and low adoption - Surprise churn from \"happy\" customers - Weak expansion despite good usage Circle one. 2. Decide Where AI Helps First Is this mainly a problem of: - Memory (no unified view of the customer) - Reasoning (poor classification and prioritisation) - Action (slow, repetitive work and weak",
      "playbooks)",
      "- Feedback (no learning from issues and churn) Circle one or two.",
      "Pick one AI-enhanced move such as: - AI-assisted ticket triage and routing - Context panels for agents (auto-assembled from systems) - AI-generated onboarding and QBR briefs - Health scoring based on usage + support + payments - Pattern analysis of churn + escalations",
      "Complete:",
      "\"In the next 90 days, we will implement a first version of _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _.\"",
      "3. Define the Narrow Pilot Answer:",
      "- Which customers? - A specific segment, region, or tier (e.g., mid-",
      "market accounts, or customers on Plan X) - Which channels? - Email only? Chat? Tickets from the portal? - Which team? - One support pod? One CSM squad? Keep scope intentionally small.",
      "4. Set Concrete Metrics Pick 2-3 metrics that this pilot should improve:",
      "- For support: - Time to first response",
      "- Time to resolution - CSAT / effort score - Ticket volume per customer (for repeated issues) - For success: - Time-to-value for new customers - Health score stability - Expansion/churn in pilot group vs control Complete:",
      "\"We'll know this is working if, within 90 days, _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ improves from _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ to _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ (or better).\"",
      "5. Add Guardrails Write down:",
      "- What AI will not be allowed to do (e.g., offer refunds, change contract terms, send messages to strategic accounts without review).",
      "- How humans can override or pause the system. - How you'll monitor for weird failures or customer",
