      "5. Visibility & Control: Cockpit for the Physical World",
      "As you apply AI across planning, scheduling, quality, and inventory, something becomes possible:",
      "A near-real-time operational cockpit that actually means something.",
      "Instead of:",
      "- Endless static reports - Fragmented views by function - Surprises in every review meeting You target a cockpit that shows:",
      "- Today's key flows: - Orders, production, shipments, incidents - Health indicators: - Capacity utilisation - Stock levels on critical items - On-time performance - Risk indicators: - Anomalies flagged - Suppliers under watch - Routes or plants with rising incident rates AI supports this by:",
      "- Prioritising what to show: - \"These are the 10 exceptions today that deserve",
      "leadership attention.\" - Summarising: - \"Here's what changed since yesterday.\" - \"Here are emerging patterns from the last 30",
      "days.\" You stop managing operations with rear-view mirrors and gut feel and start steering with current, structured signals.",
      "Where AI Should Not Drive Ops Decisions (Yet)",
      "Some temptations to resist:",
      "1. Fully automated decisions with catastrophic downside",
