      "4. One-off pilots with no integration - A brilliant demand model runs in a separate tool. - Planners still live in Excel and ERP.",
      "Result: nice slideware, no behavioural change. Antidote:",
      "- Insist that any AI initiative: - Connects to existing systems - Changes real workflows - Has an owner and a maintenance plan",
      "Flight Exercise: Your 90-Day",
      "Operations AI Upgrade",
      "Time to bring this down from \"supply chain strategy\" to something you can actually move in a quarter. Take 20 minutes and work through this.",
      "1. Name the Most Expensive Pain",
      "Complete: \"Right now, the single most expensive or disruptive weakness in our operations/supply chain is _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _.\"",
      "Examples: - Chronic stock-outs on key items - High, sticky inventory levels - Unreliable delivery times - Constant rescheduling and overtime in production - Frequent quality escapes or rework - Too many fire-fighting escalations",
      "Pick one. Not three. One.",
      "2. Classify It in the Brain Model",
      "Is this mainly a problem of: - Memory - we don't have clean, timely visibility of reality - Reasoning - we don't forecast or plan well - Action - our scheduling and execution are clumsy - Feedback - we don't learn from recurring issues",
