      "- Action: credit limits, approvals, hedges, investment decisions",
      "- Feedback: outcomes vs assumptions, model vs reality, learning about risk appetite",
      "We'll keep it practical, not academic.",
      "1. Memory: Making Financial Reality Less Fragmented",
      "Finance lives in data, but that data is often siloed and inconsistent.",
      "Pieces live in:",
      "- ERP and general ledger - Billing and collections systems - Bank statements - CRM and contract repositories - Excel models scattered on laptops",
      "- Schedules for leases, loans, covenants The result:",
      "- It takes too long to answer basic questions - Numbers don't match depending on who you ask - Early warning signals are buried in noise AI can't fix bad accounting. It can help you build and interrogate a cleaner financial memory.",
      "1.1 Cleaning and Reconciling Automatically",
      "AI is strong at pattern matching and text understanding.",
      "Used well, it can:",
      "- Match transactions and invoices across systems (even with messy descriptions)",
      "- Identify duplicate or suspicious entries - Reconcile bank statements faster by classifying",
      "and grouping line items - Flag inconsistencies: - \"Revenue recorded with no corresponding",
      "contract in system X.\" - \"Customer IDs differ across billing and CRM for",
