      "1.2 Enriching Financial Memory with Context",
      "Pure finance data doesn't tell you enough.",
      "- A late payment from a tiny customer vs your largest client are not the same risk.",
      "- 30 days of inventory for a fast-moving SKU vs a slow one mean different things.",
      "AI can help overlay: - Customer value (from CRM) onto AR ageing - Product and segment context onto margins - Contract terms onto cash flow expectations - Operational signals (churn risk, support issues) onto revenue forecasts",
      "This turns: \"We have X crores in receivables\"",
      "into: \"We have X crores in receivables, of which Y is low-risk, Z is structurally slow, and W is genuinely at risk given recent signals.\"",
      "Same underlying numbers. Far more actionable view.",
      "2. Reasoning: From Static Budgets to Living Scenarios",
      "Most companies still run on an annual budget like it's scripture, with occasional quarterly forecasts people half-believe. Reality doesn't care. AI can help Finance move from single-plan thinking to scenario thinking without drowning in spreadsheets.",
      "2.1 Building Scenarios Without Losing Your Mind",
      "A scenario is just:",
      "A set of assumptions about key drivers run through your model to see the impact.",
      "The problem is not scenarios; it's the effort and discipline required.",
      "AI can help with: - Identifying key drivers from your historical data: - \"These five variables explain most of the movement in revenue/cost.\" - Generating variants around them: - Base case, optimistic, pessimistic - Plus \"shock\" cases - price drops, demand dips, currency moves - Running these through your models and summarising: - Revenue, margin, EBITDA impact - Cash runway under each scenario - Covenant headroom/shrinkage - Areas of concentration risk",
      "The output is not a mystical forecast. It is a map of outcomes under different assumptions.",
      "Leadership conversations shift from: - \"Is this the right number?\"",
