      "It might be: - Detailed hiring success signals - Machine failure precursors - Customer behaviour before big purchases - Early risk signals in finance or health or operations",
      "You're not just \"collecting everything\". You're designing your future training set.",
      "Move 3 - Close the Loop in the Product / Service",
      "Don't just analyse data in decks. Bake learning back into:",
      "- Scoring models - Recommendations - Pricing - Workflows - Support flows Customers then: - Experience improvements directly - Feed more data into the loop - Become more dependent on your system's \"way",
      "of doing things\" This is not \"we sent a monthly report\". This is \"the system got better without them having to ask.\"",
      "Move 4 - Review the Loop at the Top Table",
      "At least twice a year, leadership should explicitly ask: - Where is our advantage loop strongest? - Where is it broken? - Which competitors have loops that outcompete ours? - What new data sources, features, or partnerships could strengthen our loop?",
      "This keeps AI advantage: - Out of IT-only thinking - Firmly inside strategy conversations",
      "4. Portfolio of Bets: Core, Adjacent, and Wildcards",
      "In an AI-turbulent world, a single big bet is suicidal.",
      "You need a portfolio:",
      "1. Core bets - strengthen existing businesses with AI",
      "- Horizon 1-2 - Improve cost, speed, reliability, customer",
