      "- Agents interacting with multiple systems: - Sending emails - Editing records - Triggering workflows - No clear kill-switch, no audit trail, no owner. 1. Accountability Fog - Something goes wrong and: - Vendor blames \"model behaviour\" - Internal tech blames \"business requirements\" - Business blames \"black box\" - No one is actually accountable. Governance is the boring, necessary work of: - Admitting these are real - Deciding how much of each you're willing to risk - Designing guardrails that are sharp enough to",
      "matter and light enough to live with",
      "2. Five Non-Negotiable Principles (Spoken in Human Language)",
